<article class="env-lemma" id="04GS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04GS">Lemma <span data-tag="04GS">10.155.6</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a local map of local rings. Let $R \to R^ h$ and $S \to S^ h$ be the henselizations. There exists a unique local ring map $R^ h \to S^ h$ fitting into the commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ R^ h \ar[r]_ f &  S^ h \\  R \ar[u] \ar[r] &  S \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/08HR" data-tag="08HR">10.154.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>